**Group commits by Pending Implementation (PI).** Each PI from [Dev Notes]{{ mention: page:37db2572-f788-81db-aa87-d189be40b121 }} gets a bold-text heading that **exactly matches** its task title (e.g. `**PI-1: Task Title**`). List the commits belonging to that PI underneath. **PIs appear in order (PI-1, PI-2, …) and commit numbers stay globally sequential across all PIs — no reset.** Each PI may contain one or more commits.
  **Break implementation into atomic, standalone commits.** Each commit should be independently testable and deployable: the whole workspace builds and all tests pass at that commit — no forward dependencies on unmerged work. Format each commit as a subpage titled `Commit N: type(scope): description` following conventional commit style. Include Scope, Description, file tree, and file content sections within.
  - ⏳ — Pending / in progress
  - ✅ — Merged / complete
  - 🛑 — Blocked by another commit (note the dependency)
  **Keep PI headings in sync with Dev Notes** — if a PI is renamed, update the heading here in the same edit.
